lines+=['', '## Every transition and wrap','', '- Idle f0→1→2→3→4→5→6→7: consistently lowered hands, similar torso volume, arms and leg bend. Small breathing shifts of roughly 1–2px; no obvious global scale jump. f7→f0 returns smoothly in the ordered frame comparison, except the unresolved source toe contour. This is frame-by-frame sequence review, not in-game playback or a runtime contact check.', '- light3 f0→1 lifts the bent knee; 1→2 extends the kick; 2→3 holds the extension; 3→4 retracts and raises the crown from about y23 to y12; 4→5 plants the foot; 5→6 settles. H estimates stay 31–35px through these poses. The 11px positional change remains visible but is not itself a proven size change: head lengths and body orientation must be considered separately. Endpoint f6→f0 changes from two feet planted to knee lift; anims.json declares this non-looping, so that is a preview replay seam, not an engine wrap defect. Hand-pocket pose and twisted torso prevent a strict full-segment pass.', '- airRecover f0→1 rotates from tucked back pose to inverted tuck; 1→2 opens arms and legs for recovery. Each frame is an intact figure. The dramatic projected torso/limb differences track rotation and occlusion; no equivalent reference view exists to certify exact lengths. f2→f0 resets from open recovery to tuck; this strip is non-looping. No seamless looping claim is made.', '', '## Idle f7 shoe edge recheck', '', '[Source boundary crop](idle-source-f7-edge.png): original source is 2172×724. Crop is x1892:2172,y480:724, enlarged3×. The right shoe visibly intersects x2171; it is not merely a detached background speck. Its missing extent cannot be inferred from the clipped source. Actual packed f7 has transparent margins and surviving shoe endpoints around (150,235)→(181,235), so it is not a new atlas-edge clip. Atlas margin does not restore a source-cut toe. Retain technical HOLD; this does not reject the accepted stance.', '', '## Interpretation', '', 'Idle torso and general build visually track the neutral cell; no old guard-envelope requirement is applied. Different stance changes leg projections and shoulder presentation. Light3 upright recovery torso chord is about70px versus neutral79px, while bent frames are about62–65px versus combat71px: these differences are residual projections under uncertain garment landmarks, not a certified anatomical shortening. AirRecover lacks pose-matched length evidence throughout; shoe lengths vary with viewing angle and overlapping soles. The supplied 6% criterion cannot be certified for all requested segments on any strip from these rasters; no fabricated numeric passes or new calibration overrides are issued.', '', 'Other Gojo strips were not re-audited. Older round4 numbers belong to their recorded atlas/calibration and must not be silently attributed to this atlas. Runtime contacts/hurtboxes remain Claude-owned. Build is not an anatomy test and was not rerun for these audit-only evidence files.', '', '## Immutable input hashes', '']
